The copied engine lives in liquidglass/src/main/kotlin/io/github/ntvien/liquidglass/internal/backdrop.
GlassInteraction.kt and Droplet.kt are ported from the AndroidLiquidGlass catalog
(InteractiveHighlight.kt, DragGestureInspector.kt, LiquidButton.kt, DampedDragAnimation.kt, LiquidBottomTabs.kt).

Changes made to the original code:
  1. Package renamed (com.kyant.backdrop -> io.github.ntvien.liquidglass.internal.backdrop), expect/actual merged
     (Android only), every declaration made internal.
  2. DrawBackdropModifier.kt: the backdrop is re-recorded only when the element's position in the window changes,
     not on every relayout.
  3. ShadowModifier.kt, InnerShadowModifier.kt, HighlightModifier.kt: shadow, inner shadow and highlight layers are
     recorded only when size, shape or parameters other than alpha change (internal/RecordKey.kt, new file); alpha
     is set on the layer without re-recording.
  4. RuntimeShaderCache.kt: AGSL shaders are compiled once per key and shared by all glass elements.
  5. internal/Paint.kt: deprecated asFrameworkPaint() replaced by nativePaint.
  6. GlassInteraction.kt, Droplet.kt: spring parameters exposed, optional blur on the droplet, wrapped for reuse.
  7. highlight/HighlightStyle.kt: corner radii of continuous shapes (RoundedRectangularShape) are read from the shape
     instead of falling back to a capsule.
  8. effects/Lens.kt, internal/Shaders.kt: the refraction shaders take a saturation uniform, so the vibrancy color
     filter (effects/ColorFilter.kt) is applied inside the lens pass instead of as a separate pass before it.
